This project is inspired by the distributed inference architecture of
Petals (BigScience workshop, https://github.com/bigscience-workshop/petals),
released under the MIT License. Diffuse reimplements these concepts from
scratch and shares no source code with Petals.

Diffuse extends the distributed-inference model with a privacy layer
(trusted execution, context threat model), a contribution-incentive layer
(usage credit), and product-grade deployment (self-configuring daemon,
private-team mode).